Encode an SDR output with gamma 2.2, not sRGB

Problem: without an output image description, Wayfire encodes the output with
the sRGB curve. It advertises gamma 2.2 to clients as the output's preferred
description, decodes untagged surfaces as gamma 2.2, and its software cursor
uses gamma 2.2. In dark tones the two curves do not cancel out: every
composited window is darkened (measured: (30,31,34) shows as (24,25,28)),
while a directly scanned-out game shows its real values. A fullscreen game
then looks "muted" next to the desktop, and its colors change when Wayfire
toggles between scanout and composition.
Fix: the SDR default transfer function is gamma 2.2, so gamma 2.2 and untagged
content passes through unchanged and matches direct scanout.
Upstream: not reported yet.
Remove when: upstream encodes SDR outputs with gamma 2.2 (or matches what it
advertises). Check: nested Wayfire with WLR_RENDERER=vulkan, a GTK window with
background #1e1f22; grim must read (30,31,34).
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

